On Nov 29, 10:59 am, "John H." <Joh...@gmail.com> wrote:
> On Nov 28, 10:16 am, pend...@hotmail.com wrote:
>
> > I'm pondering the possibility of -- purely for my own enjoyment,
> > although I might post it if anyone else wanted it -- building a Narnia-
> > themed Quest.
>
> One of my favorite things about Nethack is how gleefully it ransacks
> fantasy literature, from Terry Pratchett to Tolkien to Edmund Spenser,
> so I'm generally in favor of adding Narnia stuff to the game so long
> as it stays on the side of being more fun and fantastic and less
> overtly Christian.
>
> If it were done as a quest, however, putting a made-up figure into the
> neutral role simply wouldn't do.  Because Nethack's mechanics demand a
> neutral deity, and because I can't really think of a good role that
> would match Narnia deities (Knight is taken, and its quest artifact,
> the Magic Mirror of Merlin, is one of the most awesome references in
> the game), I'd suggest that it not be turned into a role.
>
> Think about it a bit.  There's all kinds of things in Nethack to serve
> as inspiration.  Elbereth (and lots of other stuff) is from Tolkien,
> long worms from Dune, towels from Hitchhiker's Guide to the Galaxy, a
> number of things from Discworld... I'd suggest adding something along
> those lines, maybe a special monster, maybe a neat game element, maybe
> a (normal) artifact.

A good point. The OP's "wood between the worlds" accessed by an
artifact ring (or a wardrobe portal, or something else) could be
implemented without all the additional baggage of a class and quest
and deities and everything else.


